-Tersmette1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tersmette</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruters</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>de Wolf</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>de Goede</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Lange</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Evidence for a role of virulent human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) variants in the pathogenesis of acquired immunodeficiency syndrome: studies on sequential HIV isolates.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>63</volume><fpage>2118</fpage><lpage>2125</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2564898</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000377-Tersmette2"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tersmette</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lange</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>de Goede</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>de Wolf</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Eeftink-Schattenkerk</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Association between biological properties of human immunodeficiency virus variants and risk for AIDS and AIDS mortality.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>983</fpage><lpage>985</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2565516</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000377-Allen1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Connor</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>Jing</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Dzuris</surname><given-names>JL</g